# Spring Boot backend conventions

## Stack

- Java 21, Spring Boot, Spring Web, Spring Security, Spring Data JPA, Flyway, PostgreSQL, Redis (configured, features later)

## Structure

- `config/` — security, Redis, framework configuration
- `common/` — cross-cutting concerns (`exception`, `response`, `validation`)
- Feature packages (e.g. `incident/`) are added in later phases — do not create them prematurely

## Coding rules

- Constructor injection only
- Thin controllers; business logic in services (when introduced)
- DTOs at API boundaries; never expose JPA entities directly from REST
- Repositories handle persistence
- Use Bean Validation on request DTOs
- Use transactions deliberately in services
- Avoid unnecessary abstractions and premature microservices

## Configuration

- Use environment variables for DB and Redis (see `backend/.env.example`)
- Separate `application-test.yml` for tests
- Flyway migrations live in `src/main/resources/db/migration/`
